  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 217 AM EDT Fri Oct 30 2026\n\n- Slight Chances for Rain Saturday\n\nWhile chances for rain are low Saturday (20 percent) there are\nsome synoptic features that could support some showers creeping\ninto the area during the morning and afternoon. First there will \nbe upper level support with the right entrance region of the jet \nproviding a source of upper level divergence. Then the warm air \nand moisture advection from 850-700mb. The dry surface layer may \nprevent rain from reaching the ground our limit light showers to \nsprinkles. However some sounding profiles show deep moisture \naloft, therefore worth keeping a mention of showers in the \nforecast, particularly in southwest Michigan where we'll be on the\nedge of a shortwave and positive vorticity advection that will \nslowly shift east through the weekend.\n\n- Mild with Rain Chances Next Week\n\nWhile the overall pattern remains murky next week, southwest flow\nwill bring mild temperatures and additional chances for rain. A \nmid-level ridge may keep dry conditions in place for Monday but \nlowering heights and southwest flow will reintroduce rain chances \nto the area Monday night into Tuesday. The overall trough feature \nstill has spread in the timing, placement, and strength, therefore\nthe NBM is painting continuous rain chances through next week. \nThis doesn't mean nonstop rain for several days. The main feature \nfor these rain chances moves over the CONUS Sunday and with better\nsampling we should see guidance hone in on a similar scenario. \nOverall expect confidence in the extended to increase toward the \nlatter half of the weekend.\n\nHighs next week will mostly be in the mid 60s to low 70s with lows\nin the 40s and 50s. Normal temperatures this time of year are in\nthe 50s with lows in the 30s.",
